>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_backend`

``` hol4
Refute.register_backend : backend -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces a Refute search backend.

The public backend type has the following record shape:

``` hol4
type backend =
  {name : string,
   weight : int,
   configured : unit -> bool,
   requires : requirement,
   input : goal_form,
   run : config -> instance list -> outcome}
```

Registrations are session-local.  A later backend with the same `name`
replaces the old one.  Eligible backends are ordered by increasing
`weight`, then name.  `configured` is queried when selecting a search;
`requires` is `AnyGoal`, `ExecutableGoal`, or
`ExecutableGoalUnless predicate`.  The last accepts an executable goal or,
when `predicate cfg instances` is true, a non-executable one.  `input`
requests either `MonoInstances` or `PolyOriginal` instances.

`register_backend backend` assigns the conservative certainty ceiling
`Genuine`.  This is safe for every backend but may make a race wait after
a weaker result.  Backends that can declare a tighter ceiling should use
`register_backend_with_ceiling`.

The callback's exceptions and ordinary timeouts are converted to
`Unknown`; interrupts are re-raised.

### See also

[`register_backend_with_ceiling`](#Refute.register_backend_with_ceiling),
[`Refute.register_substrate`](#Refute.register_substrate),
[`Refute.config`](#Refute.config),
[`Refute.refute`](#Refute.refute)

The extension model is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
